      "id": "PRH-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "anchor": "inputs-overlap-smooth-separation",
      "title": "Smooth cutoff thickening in the positive cone, lattice dilation count, and smoothness of the dyadic retraction",
      "hypotheses": "Arbitrary number field L; integer rank N ≥ 0 for smooth bump separation and lattice dilation count, and N ≥ 1 for the dyadic retraction; finite-dimensional real normed space HS(L, N) of Hermitian matrix tuples with positive-definite cone Pos(L, N), quadratic form q_h(z) = ∑_w Re(z_w* h_w z_w) on V_ℝ = ∏_w ℂ^N of real dimension d_ℝ, arithmetic group Γ = GL_N(𝒪_L) acting by q_{γ·h}(z) = q_h(γ⁻¹ z), L_θ-Lipschitz smooth cutoff θ : ℝ → [0, 1] equal to 1 on (−∞, 1] and 0 on [4, ∞), single-scale outer-product average T_s(h) = (s² Z_s(h))⁻¹ ∑_{v∈𝒪_L^N} θ(q_h(v)/s) rk(h, v), and (for N ≥ 1) smooth Γ-invariant proxy μ : Pos(L, N) → ℝ satisfying c_μ λ∨(h) ≤ μ(h) ≤ C′_μ λ∨(h) with c_μ > 0.",
      "statement": "For N ≥ 0, every compact subset K ⊆ Pos(L, N) admits ε > 0 with compact closed metric thickening K′ ⊆ Pos(L, N) ({x : dist(x, K) ≤ ε} for K ≠ ∅, ∅ for K = ∅), a constant m > 0, and b ∈ C^∞(HS(L, N), ℝ) supported in K′ satisfying 0 ≤ b ≤ 1/m and b ≥ 1 on K, so every smooth function supported in K′ (in particular ψ = b/g(S) extended by zero) has a global Lipschitz constant L_ψ; for N ≥ 0, α ∈ ℝ, h ∈ Pos(L, N), and s ≥ 0, #{v ∈ 𝒪_L^N : q_h(v) ≤ α s} ≤ (√(8 max(α, 1) + 2))^{d_ℝ} #{v ∈ 𝒪_L^N : q_h(v) ≤ s}; and for N ≥ 1, R(h) = μ(h) h + ∑_{j∈ℤ} θ(4^j μ(h)) T_{4^j}(h) maps Pos(L, N) into Pos(L, N), satisfies R(γ·h) = γ·R(h) and q_{R(h)}(z) ≥ μ(h) q_h(z), and is C^∞ on Pos(L, N) via local truncation to a finite window of scales and lattice vectors F₀ ⊂ 𝒪_L^N.",
      "definitions": [
        "closed metric thickening K′ ⊆ Pos(L, N) ({x ∈ HS(L, N) : dist(x, K) ≤ ε} when K ≠ ∅, ∅ when K = ∅) and rescaled smooth seed b = f/m (m = min_{x∈K} f(x) > 0 for K ≠ ∅, b = 0 and m = 1 for K = ∅)",
        "lattice dilation constant C_α = (√(8 max(α, 1) + 2))^{d_ℝ} on V_ℝ of real dimension d_ℝ = dim_ℝ V_ℝ",
        "single-scale rank-one average T_s(h) = (s² Z_s(h))⁻¹ ∑_{v∈𝒪_L^N} θ(q_h(v)/s) rk(h, v) with Z_s(h) = ∑_{v∈𝒪_L^N} θ(q_h(v)/s) ≥ 1 and dyadic retraction R(h) = μ(h) h + ∑_{j∈ℤ} θ(4^j μ(h)) T_{4^j}(h)"
      ],
